      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To file a roof insurance claim in Utah, start with an independent inspection and document all damage before contacting your insurance company.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step-by-Step Claim Process"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Get an Independent Inspection: Have a trusted, licensed local roofer inspect your roof first. They can tell you if the damage actually warrants filing a claim (avoiding unnecessary claims that raise your rates). Services like Master Roofing can assist with storm damage evaluations and meeting adjusters on-site.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Document the Damage: Take wide and close-up photos of the roof, and check for interior issues (water stains, wet insulation, peeling paint). Note the date of the storm (hail, wind, or heavy snow) and keep timestamps.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "File the Claim: Contact your insurance carrier to open the claim.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Meet the Adjuster: Be present\u2014or have your roofing contractor present\u2014when the insurance adjuster inspects the roof to point out all damage and ensure items are not missed.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Utah Deadlines & Laws"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Reporting Window: Most Utah policies require you to report damage \"promptly\" (frequently within 30 days to a year depending on the specific policy language).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Insurers' Timelines: Under Utah law, the insurance company must acknowledge your claim within 10 business days and complete their investigation within 45 days of receiving documentation.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Statute of Limitations: You have 6 years from the date of loss to file a lawsuit if there is a claim dispute.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Important Consumer Protections & Warnings"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Deductible Laws: Be careful with contractors who offer to \"waive\" or cover your insurance deductible\u2014this can be illegal under Utah law.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Avoid Scams: Never sign away your insurance rights to a third party or pay high upfront deposits. If you spot or suspect contractor fraud, report it to the Utah Insurance Department .",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
                "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/roofing-scams-hail-yes/"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Denied Claims: If your claim is denied or under-scoped, you can request a re-inspection, gather more photo evidence, or work through a supplement process.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4,
              6
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help you figure out your next move, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What kind of weather caused the damage (hail, high wind, heavy snow, or a leak)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Has an adjuster already inspected the property?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
